Nele and I are sitting in the office by the window.
The coffee is sitting between us.
We also have the laptop open.
The big design project is completely normal everyday life now.
We are discussing our tasks.
Nele points at the screen.
"The new colors look really good, Maya," she says.
"Thank you," I reply.
I take a sip and look outside.
The trees have thick, green leaves.
The weather is wonderfully warm.
I briefly think back to January.
Back then, the branches were completely bare.
It was so cold and dark in Berlin.
The new job was exciting, but also a little daunting.
Everything was so unfamiliar to me back then.
"Is everything okay?" Nele asks.
She looks at me questioningly.
"Yes, everything is great," I say.
"I am just happy about the summer."
